        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Handler Returns"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "plain return fulfills the derived promise",
            "return a promise — the chain waits",
            "resolve(thenable) adopts its eventual state",
            "resolve chains unwrap, hop by hop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Thenables & Adoption"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Any object with a `.then` method is treated promise-like. The machinery only needs `.then` to subscribe."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "const wait = ms =>",
            "  new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, ms));",
            "const read = f =>",
            "  fs.promises.readFile(f, 'utf8');",
            "await wait(500); // callback-free"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Never Synchronous",
          "text": "`then` handlers always queue as microtasks — they never run inline, even on an already-settled promise."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Tick Of The Loop",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "macrotask runs",
              "drain microtasks",
              "render",
              "next macrotask"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "javascript",
          "lines": [
            "async function* pages(url) {",
            "  const p = await fetchPage(url);",
            "  yield p.items; // yield may await",
            "  if (p.next) yield* pages(p.next);",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
